Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the loader not handling cases where keyspaces contained no user-defined types (UDTs). The previous implementation did not account for an empty collection of UDTs, leading to potential errors or failures during the loading process. This oversight prevented the loader from functioning correctly when it encountered keyspaces without any user types.

